2026-11-23  G. Branden Robinson <g.branden.robinson@gmail.com>

	* src/roff/troff/input.cpp: Revise identifier error diagnostics.
	Much as we'd like to, we can't say what the consequence of an
	invalid identifier is; some requests, like `rm`, `rr`, and the
	dumpers (`pchar`, `pev`, etc.) skip over them; others abort
	their operation.  Some pretend that the invalid identifier isn't
	there and perform a surprising alternative operation (see, e.g.,
	Savannah #68954), but I am steadily removing that form of "error
	handling" from GNU troff.
	(diagnose_invalid_identifier, read_input_until_terminator): Drop
	potentially misleading gerunds from error messages.

2026-11-23  G. Branden Robinson <g.branden.robinson@gmail.com>

	* src/roff/troff/env.cpp (environment_switch_request): Recast
	diagnostic to make more conceptual sense; while "underflow" is a
	technically correct description, the user is unlikely to know
	that GNU troff stacks only environments that _aren't_ current;
	*roff documentation in general suggests that only a simple stack
	data structure (or equivalent) is used, without special storage
	for the current environment "on deck"; and a forthcoming
	refactoring is going to make that simpler arrangement effective
	in GNU troff regardless.

