2026-11-16  G. Branden Robinson <g.branden.robinson@gmail.com>

	* src/preproc/pic/lex.cpp (yylex): Fix code style nit.  Return
	zero of character type (`\0`) rather than integer.  The
	idiomatic use of lex/flex is deliberately slovenly typed,
	assuming a 7- or 8-bit character type and package a bunch of
	integral token identifiers into the copious headroom in an `int`
	beyond the range of a valid `char`.  Nothing bad could possibly
	happen when your fundamental character type is actually wider
	and has values that collide with your token identifiers, which
	could have been in an `enum` but aren't.  Real Programmers don't
	need data types.  At any rate I intend this change to help the
	reader grasp that the `0` literal here is not a null pointer
	constant, which it idiomatically can be in ISO C++98.

2026-11-16  G. Branden Robinson <g.branden.robinson@gmail.com>

	* src/preproc/pic/lex.cpp: Fix code style nits.  Drop names of
	unambiguous parameters from member function declarations,
	Stroustrup-style.  Parenthesize formally complex expressions.
	Arrange equality comparisons to avoid inadvertent assignment to
	lvalue.  Explicitly compare variable of pointer type to ISO
	C++98 null pointer literal, instead of punning it down to a
	Boolean.  Compare unsigned integral types to explicitly unsigned
	integer literals.

